  "term": "VMH",
  "definition": "VMH stands for the ventromedial nucleus of the hypothalamus, a brain region examined in research on stress, pain, and fear-related biological responses. In the supplied source, it is one of the hypothalamic areas where changes in CRF receptor gene expression were studied after early-life pain and later fear conditioning.",
